{"name":"Snap-Shot","hex":"#2b3e52","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snap-shot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of snap shot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snap-shot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snapshot (photography)","blocks":[{"text":"A snapshot is a photograph that is \"shot\" spontaneously and quickly, most often without artistic or journalistic intent and usually made with a relatively cheap and compact camera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Schreck.JPG/330px-Schreck.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snapshot_(photography)","wikidata":"Q1758746"},{"title":"Snapshot (computer storage)","blocks":[{"text":"In computer systems, a snapshot is the state of a system at a particular point in time. The term was coined as an analogy to that in photography."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snapshot_(computer_storage)","wikidata":"Q252683"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Snapshot-baby-antics.jpg/500px-Snapshot-baby-antics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Snapshot-baby-antics.jpg/1280px-Snapshot-baby-antics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Snapshot-baby-antics.jpg/500px-Snapshot-baby-antics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snapshots render memorable moments in imperfect images. Here, glare exposes the photographer and implies a close and familiar relationship to the subject.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnapshot-baby-antics.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Tourist_taking_selfie_in_2016%2C_City_Hall_garden%2C_Stockholm%2C_Swed